The graph shows the balance owing on a reducing balance loan.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=9.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=190,ymin=0,ymax=130000,xtick={0,30,60,90,120,150,180},ytick={0,20000,40000,60000,80000,100000,120000},grid=both,samples=80,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Months},ylabel={Balance owing (\$)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue,domain=0:180]{120000*(3.83805 - exp(x*0.00747198))/2.83805};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use the graph to estimate how much is still owing after $120$ months.
